## Day Learning Log – Network Technologies in Home

Today I learned about network technologies used in home networks and different types of network cables such as coaxial cable, twisted pair cable, and optical fiber cable.

### Coaxial Cable
- Used in cable TV and broadband connections
- Contains single copper conductor with insulation
- Provides good protection from noise
- Used in older Ethernet networks

### Twisted Pair Cable
- Most commonly used cable in home networks
- Contains twisted copper wires
- Types: UTP (Unshielded Twisted Pair) and STP (Shielded Twisted Pair)
- Used in LAN and Ethernet connections

### Optical Fiber Cable
- Uses light signals to transmit data
- Very high speed communication
- Used in modern internet connections
- Best for long distance networking

### Key Takeaways
- Different cables are used in home networking
- Twisted pair is the most common
- Optical fiber is the fastest
- Coaxial cable is used in TV and broadband
